<i>After having it pointed out to me 
by this Yukimura person,</i>

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:26.680
<i>I did some calculations.</i>

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:29.430
<i>Back then, I tripped...</i>

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:32.040
<b>Kanade-san: mass X</b>

00:13:30.020 --> 00:13:32.140
<i>and ended up in this sort of position.</i>

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:37.750
<b>Kanade-san: mass X</b>

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:37.750
<b>Me: mass m</b>

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:34.980
<i>If I had continued falling in that manner,</i>

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:37.760
<i>my right hand would have... um...</i>

00:13:39.210 --> 00:13:42.630
<i>Kanade-kun, there is a very high probability 
that I would have touched your right breast.</i>

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:45.380
What did you make my teacher do?!

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:50.870
<i>It may already have become 
a painful memory for you,</i>

00:13:50.870 --> 00:13:53.330
<i>but, if possible, I don't want 
you to think of it that way.</i>

00:13:54.320 --> 00:13:55.390
<i>Because, for me...</i>

00:13:55.960 --> 00:14:00.080
<i>the days I spent in study with you...</i>

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:03.230
<i>were truly, truly enjoyable.</i>

00:14:04.390 --> 00:14:06.520
<i>I'm glad I met you.</i>

00:14:06.790 --> 00:14:09.920
<i>That's the one thing I want to say to you.</i>

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:27.050
<b>Professor of the University Lab to Which Kanade Kotonoha Is Affiliated</b>

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:14.660
<i>Well, about Kanade-kun...</i>

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:19.960
<i>Ever since I first met her I had the 
sense that she was a powerful one.</i>

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:22.920
<i>I'd like to keep this a secret from her,</i>

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:27.040
<i>but if possible, I'd like to ask 
her to spar with me, just once.</i>

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:34.180
<b>A Lazy Senpai From Kanade Kotonoha's University Lab</b>

00:14:27.940 --> 00:14:30.490
<i>If Kanade wasn't normal?</i>

00:14:28.390 --> 00:14:30.490
<i>Aika!</i>

00:14:30.490 --> 00:14:34.180
<i>What are you talking about 
here in this insane lab?</i>

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:39.690
<b>A Pervert in the University Lab to Which Kanade Kotonoha Is Affiliated</b>

00:14:35.840 --> 00:14:39.680
<i>Come back and ask that again after 
she's crazier than that guy is.</i>

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:53.950
<b>A Senpai in the University Lab to Which Kanade Kotonoha Is Affiliated</b>

00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:42.050
<i>Kanade-chan is...</i>

00:14:42.510 --> 00:14:45.070
<i>It's true that she's cheerful and cute,</i>

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:47.490
<i>and she's always conscientious 
of the people around her.</i>

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:49.350
<i>I like those parts of her, too, but...</i>

00:14:49.830 --> 00:14:53.940
<i>I've felt like she holds herself back, like 
there's a part of her she doesn't want to show.</i>

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:58.980
<i>Personally, it would make me happy 
if she'd lean on me a little more.</i>

00:14:58.980 --> 00:15:01.830
<i>I want to know all about Kanade-chan.</i>

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:12.090
Aika...
I love you...

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:12.090
<b>Happy</b>

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:12.090
She's more
efficient that way

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:12.090
Doesn't matter

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:12.090
<b>Fig. 2.3:  Distribution of Reactions of Those Around Kanade Kotonoha
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hto the Parts of Her Which Are Not Normal</b>

00:15:02.860 --> 00:15:07.470
As this shows, in the expression of points 
Kanade considers to be "not normal,"

00:15:07.470 --> 00:15:11.760
affirmative opinions such as "Happy" and 
"Doesn't matter" constituted the majority.

00:15:12.070 --> 00:15:15.170
Kanade's high level of popularity 
and her character as a person...

00:15:15.170 --> 00:15:16.770
<i>Yukimura-senpai...</i>

00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:19.930
<i>have you been collecting data 
like this all this time?</i>

00:15:19.930 --> 00:15:21.330
<i>For my sake?</i>

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:22.220
In short,

00:15:22.220 --> 00:15:24.110
as one can understand from this data,

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:26.090
the concept of "normal" is—

00:15:29.050 --> 00:15:32.120
You came in right when we 
were starting to have fun,

00:15:32.120 --> 00:15:34.970
then showed us some confusing 
slides and videos.

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:36.620
I'm not following, you know?

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:40.130
He's so weak! And he came alone?

00:15:40.130 --> 00:15:42.770
Shikijou-kun, that's enough, right?

00:15:42.770 --> 00:15:44.390
Let's hurry up and beat him to a pulp.

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:47.510
I see. That's right.

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:50.400
You have to read the room.

00:15:50.400 --> 00:15:54.380
This has nothing to do with you. 
What did you come here for?

00:15:54.380 --> 00:15:56.900
If you think about it normally, 
it goes against common sense!

00:15:56.900 --> 00:15:58.270
Yukimura-senpai!

00:15:58.270 --> 00:15:59.420
Take that!

00:15:58.650 --> 00:16:00.230
Yukimura-senpai!

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:01.030
There you go.

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:01.980
Yukimura-senpai!

00:16:08.460 --> 00:16:11.560
Th-Those things known as 
"normal" and "common sense,"

00:16:11.980 --> 00:16:14.270
...are relative concepts.

00:16:14.580 --> 00:16:18.150
In the same way that what these guys 
call "normal" can appear atypical...

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:22.160
<b>Set of Special Characteristics of Individuals' Concept of Normal</b>

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:22.160
<b></b>A's concept of normal

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:22.160
<b></b>B's concept of normal

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:22.160
<b></b>C's concept of normal

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:22.160
<b></b>Area of commonality between the 3 people

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:22.690
the contents of a set of normality, 
depending on each individual...

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:24.790
w-will differ...

00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:28.550
You understand that now, don't you, Kanade?

00:16:29.410 --> 00:16:32.550
Shut up! You're just a four-eyes 
who studies too hard!

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:34.860
Are you trying to be a hero 
of justice or something?

00:16:34.860 --> 00:16:38.440
What can you do on your own, you moron?

00:16:38.650 --> 00:16:41.120
<i>Stop... Stop!</i>

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:44.680
<i>Why? Why would he go so far?</i>

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:50.770
What? You gonna pull out a gun or something?

00:16:50.770 --> 00:16:51.560
Huh?

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:54.450
You...

00:16:54.450 --> 00:16:55.830
What're you trying to do?

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:58.530
Do you know what this is?

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:03.550
You should have seen it once in 
a middle school science class.

00:17:04.520 --> 00:17:06.580
Is that... It can't be!

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:08.090
<b>Concentrated Sulfuric Acid</b>

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:10.590
<b>Concentrated Hydrochloric Acid</b>

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:10.590
<b>Concentrated Nitric Acid</b>

00:17:10.790 --> 00:17:12.950
I borrowed them from the science department.

00:17:12.950 --> 00:17:15.930
They're strong acids that can eventually 
eat away a whole human body.

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:17.940
If any of it happened 
to adhere to your skin,

00:17:17.940 --> 00:17:20.850
you must rinse it off under running 
water as quickly as possible.

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:23.380
Wait! Wait! Wait! Wait! Wait! 
That's super dangerous!

00:17:23.380 --> 00:17:25.230
Why are you carrying stuff like that?

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:26.600
What are you talking about?

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:30.360
On the grounds of a single university...

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:33.850
do you know just how many toxic substances 
and dangerous objects there are?

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:35.720
Remember this:

00:17:35.720 --> 00:17:37.610
When you bare your fangs 
at a science-type...

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:40.710
you make all of these things your enemies!

00:17:41.840 --> 00:17:44.120
It got on my clothes!

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:46.210
Th-This isn't funny!

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:49.120
You can't expect me to go up 
against someone that insane!

00:17:50.030 --> 00:17:51.990
I'm out, Shikijou!

00:17:52.730 --> 00:17:53.380
Wai—

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:54.910
Hurry up! Water! Water!

00:17:54.450 --> 00:17:55.520
Wait!

00:17:54.910 --> 00:17:56.370
Outside! Head outside!

00:18:07.030 --> 00:18:10.090
Who on earth are you?

00:18:10.090 --> 00:18:12.650
There's something wrong with 
your head! You're not normal!

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:15.260
Why are you getting in my way?

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:18.280
I only wanted to have a normal romance!

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:19.830
Shikijou Naoya.

00:18:20.190 --> 00:18:23.060
A person like you is exactly 
the same as the research

00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:25.420
you presented at the Okinawa research camp.

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:29.390
All you did was make the outward 
appearance seem all right,

00:18:29.390 --> 00:18:31.300
while the content was rotten 
through and through.

00:18:31.300 --> 00:18:32.490
Shut up!

00:18:32.490 --> 00:18:34.550
You're the one who isn't normal!

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:37.110
Kanade-san and I are sweethearts!

00:18:37.110 --> 00:18:39.440
And what are you? 
It's got nothing to do with you, right?

00:18:39.440 --> 00:18:40.800
Why would you go this far?

00:18:42.230 --> 00:18:43.300
Why?

00:18:44.950 --> 00:18:47.070
Why, you ask?

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:51.860
That is because you...

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:53.810
have angered a science-type!

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:01.880
It hurts! It hurts! It...

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:03.410
Huh?

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:06.480
Don't worry. It's just water.

00:19:06.480 --> 00:19:07.210
What?

00:19:07.470 --> 00:19:11.410
I could never use a dangerous 
substance like this,

00:19:11.410 --> 00:19:12.220
you moron.

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:14.210
Though, this...

00:19:14.740 --> 00:19:18.160
did allow me to buy enough time 
for the police to arrive.

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:17.100
Hey, lemme go!

00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:19.290
What's all this all of a sudden?

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:20.340
What are you saying we did?

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:20.590
Hey, that hurts!

00:19:21.160 --> 00:19:22.270
Let's head back...

00:19:22.270 --> 00:19:23.210
Kanade.

00:19:27.730 --> 00:19:30.680
Why did you come to help me?

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:33.990
I... I said all those horrible things.

00:19:33.990 --> 00:19:35.820
You call that horrible?

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:39.360
The things I normally say 
are much worse than that.

00:19:42.470 --> 00:19:45.380
The way you live is up to you.

00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:49.240
But if your obsession with normality 
causes you to agonize over things,

00:19:49.240 --> 00:19:51.620
then when you're with us, at least, 
you should live however you like.

00:19:52.070 --> 00:19:54.910
After all, we are the Ikeda Lab.

00:19:55.350 --> 00:19:58.140
Even if you become a little less normal...

00:19:58.140 --> 00:20:00.260
you won't stand out at all.

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:03.820
Wait a moment. I'll untie you.

00:20:03.820 --> 00:20:06.880
I learned a little of the theory 
of untying knots through topology.

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:09.320
Is it really all right?

00:20:09.320 --> 00:20:12.010
Even if I'm not normal?

00:20:12.010 --> 00:20:14.150
At the very least, it won't bother me.

00:20:14.150 --> 00:20:17.890
I might throw you, Yukimura-senpai. 
Is it still all right?

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:20.280
You've already done that a number of times.

00:20:21.010 --> 00:20:23.690
Train yourself so that you don't 
inadvertently throw others.

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:25.910
I can be a subject in that experiment.

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:31.720
In my heart... I make really mean 
retorts at you, Yukimura-senpai!

00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:32.660
Is that all right?

00:20:33.910 --> 00:20:36.240
Next time, say them to me directly.

00:20:36.240 --> 00:20:37.930
I'll refute them on the spot.

00:20:37.930 --> 00:20:38.570
Huh?

00:20:43.540 --> 00:20:46.350
Seriously, are you stupid?!

00:20:48.400 --> 00:20:52.310
You should just behave and go be a 
besotted couple with Himuro-senpai!

00:20:52.310 --> 00:20:54.350
You shouldn't just traipse 
in like it's nothing!

00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:57.060
The level of urgency was too different. 
Of course I came.

00:20:57.060 --> 00:20:59.660
I've never seen anyone who came 
to save someone start with slides

00:20:59.660 --> 00:21:02.190
then start scattering toxic substances!

00:21:02.190 --> 00:21:04.460
Well, I did resolve the issue, didn't I?

00:21:04.460 --> 00:21:06.760
Gathering all that data for me!

00:21:06.760 --> 00:21:09.210
Getting all beat up with 
a body like a beansprout!

00:21:09.210 --> 00:21:11.760
Why are you always so kind to me?!

00:21:11.760 --> 00:21:13.550
Do that for Himuro-senpai!

00:21:13.550 --> 00:21:16.370
Because I have Himuro, 
I can't do anything for you?

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:20.500
And you talked about "the theory of untying 
knots," but you haven't untied me at all!

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:21.810
How clumsy can you be?

00:21:21.810 --> 00:21:23.180
No one asked you!

00:21:23.180 --> 00:21:25.330
Theory and practice are different.

00:21:25.330 --> 00:21:27.000
And...

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:28.440
This hurts, Kanade.

00:21:29.020 --> 00:21:30.790
I'm so sorry!

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:45.590
Ow!

00:21:46.020 --> 00:21:47.290
What are you doing?

00:21:50.930 --> 00:21:54.910
By the way, there's something I 
want to tell you, Yukimura-kun.

00:21:55.230 --> 00:21:57.500
The results of the experiment 
at the Mutsumi Festival?

00:21:57.870 --> 00:21:58.650
In that case...

00:21:58.650 --> 00:22:00.800
Someone seems to be in love with you.

00:22:01.850 --> 00:22:03.040
You're saying this now? I already—

00:22:03.040 --> 00:22:04.180
It's Kanade-chan.

00:22:06.060 --> 00:22:06.950
What?!

00:22:07.470 --> 00:22:12.550
I'm sorry. I wasn't planning 
to say anything about it.

00:22:12.550 --> 00:22:15.270
You don't have to apologize, Kanade-chan.

00:22:15.270 --> 00:22:16.810
We talked about it, didn't we?

00:22:16.810 --> 00:22:19.340
Once you've fallen in love, 
there's nothing you can do about it.

00:22:19.720 --> 00:22:21.450
Himuro-senpai.

00:22:21.450 --> 00:22:24.860
And Yukimura-kun told you, too, didn't he?

00:22:24.860 --> 00:22:28.330
When you're with us, you should 
live however you like.

00:22:29.910 --> 00:22:31.450
Yes, but...

00:22:31.450 --> 00:22:35.330
It seems like another interesting 
something has begun.

00:22:35.330 --> 00:22:37.450
What's wrong with me?!

00:22:37.450 --> 00:22:39.190
I love Aika.

00:22:39.190 --> 00:22:40.450
And yet!

00:22:40.450 --> 00:22:43.470
Why can't I choose the True End?!

00:22:40.460 --> 00:22:43.460
<b>Let's get married!!</b>

00:22:40.460 --> 00:22:43.460
I'm in love with someone else...

00:22:43.740 --> 00:22:47.990
Does this mean that my subconscious is 
recoiling from becoming one with Aika?!

00:22:47.990 --> 00:22:50.080
What's going on, Torasuke?

00:22:50.080 --> 00:22:53.330
Did you find a fave you love 
more than Aika or something?

00:22:54.840 --> 00:22:56.640
Sh-Sh-Shut up, Ibarada!

00:22:56.640 --> 00:22:58.440
It's got nothing to do with you!

00:22:59.200 --> 00:23:00.470
What's wrong with you?

00:23:00.790 --> 00:23:02.630
You are in love,

00:23:02.630 --> 00:23:04.840
but the quantity and type are undetermined.

00:23:04.840 --> 00:23:07.020
Which means that you and I 
are in the same situation.

00:23:06.780 --> 00:23:10.990
<b>New Research Proposal

00:23:07.400 --> 00:23:10.470
We were using "favorable feeling" 
as the subject in our research.

00:23:10.470 --> 00:23:12.310
We'll be able to obtain the perfect 
data now, don't you think?

00:23:14.070 --> 00:23:15.360
To that end...

00:23:15.830 --> 00:23:17.460
you and I, Kanade-chan...

00:23:17.890 --> 00:23:20.830
will have to see who 
loves Yukimura-kun more.

00:23:20.830 --> 00:23:23.470
Yukimura-kun, between Kanade-chan and me...

00:23:23.470 --> 00:23:25.450
you will have to see who you love more.

00:23:27.440 --> 00:23:30.460
Now, shall we begin proving it?

00:23:31.550 --> 00:23:35.090
<i>Seriously. What is this besotted 
couple talking about?</i>

00:23:35.540 --> 00:23:37.150
<i>Are we going to be okay?</i>
